12064	{"artifactId":"LLD-613abdb351c2c738-s2","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-613abdb351c2c738-s2-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-14T12:43:54.657Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S002's four acceptance criteria (ac1 places + 'N from other chats ahead', ac2 cancel, ac3 resend with attachments to the back, ac4 same after reload) and FR002 (a message leaves the outbox when taken) are each designed","evidence":"DEF.md:127-130 lists ac1-ac4 and FR001-FR004 (lines 46-49). The LLD covers them: projectOutbox gives positions and aheadFromOtherChats and drops processing rows (FR002), act handles cancel/dismiss/resend, resendFrom keeps text and attachment refs and re-inserts with a new AUTOINCREMENT seq so the row joins the back, and the outbox is projected from the queue file on 'ready' and on the worker's first tick (ac4).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No non-goal is built: there is no editing or reordering of waiting messages, no interrupt, and nothing is run again without the user","evidence":"DEF.md:76-78 rules out interrupting, editing or reordering, and unattended re-runs. The only actions in the LLD are cancel, dismiss and an explicit user resend. 'outbox-retry-now' is declared for s4 and ignored by the host here. The blockedBy line (HLD.md:211 assigns it to s2) only displays state.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The store's cancel deletes only queued or retrying rows and returns false otherwise; dismiss deletes only failed or not-delivered rows; resend refuses a missing row or one in another state with 'That message can no longer be sent again.'; and an open of a newer schema throws StoreUnavailable('made by a newer plugin')","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:407-409: `DELETE FROM messages WHERE seq = ? AND state IN ('queued', 'retrying')` ... `=== 1`. :411-413 is the same for ('failed','not-delivered'). :419-420 refuses with 'That message can no longer be sent again.'. :303-304 `version > SCHEMA_VERSION` throws StoreUnavailable(`...made by a newer plugin...`).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The worker's emit catches a list() error, logs it and delivers no rows; it emits after its own writes as well as other connections' commits; and its first tick emits the file's rows (which the reload case relies on)","evidence":"chat-queue-worker.ts:85-91: emit catches store.list() errors, logs a warning and returns. noticeChanges (:103-108) compares `${dataVersion()}:${ownWrites()}` against `stamp`, which starts as '', so the first tick always emits. The store's write() increments `own` (chat-queue-store.ts:280).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The webview's doSubmit marks the turn running locally on submit, and the host already posts 'turn-running' when a queued message starts","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:1236: doSubmit posts submit-turn and then calls `setRunning(true);setProgress('working…')`. chat-panel.ts:1971 has queueRunner.run post `{ type: 'turn-running', sessionId: s.id }`, and :1207 shows the webview handling 'turn-running'.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"resendFrom, markWaiting, act, onWaiting, waitingOn and projectOutbox are new, and the reused worker/store members exist with the stated shape (submit / onChange / liveSessionIds / running / dispose; cancel / dismiss / resend(seq, newTurnId) / list)","evidence":"The ChatQueueWorker interface (chat-queue-worker.ts:42-51) has exactly submit, onChange, liveSessionIds, running and dispose. The ChatQueueStore interface (chat-queue-store.ts:92-113) has cancel, dismiss, `resend(seq, newTurnId)` (which keeps old.windowKey at :428) and list, with no resendFrom or markWaiting. QueuedMessage (:34-54) has no waitingOn. QueuedTurnRunner.run (worker.ts:31-33) takes (message, onSpawn) only.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The host can supply runningChat.here even though it does not hold the window key","evidence":"The ChatPanelHost deps carry only `queue?: (runner) => ChatQueueWorker` (chat-panel.ts:128), so the host has no claim or windowKey. Because one message runs per repository, worker.running() (chat-queue-worker.ts:229-231) is enough for the `here` predicate. resendFrom's window key comes from the worker's own claim, which the LLD states.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding an optional third parameter onWaiting to QueuedTurnRunner.run is compatible with its single implementer and its caller","evidence":"The only implementation is chat-panel.ts:1955-1982 `run(message, onSpawn)`. The only caller is runMessage at chat-queue-worker.ts:139. An optional trailing parameter does not break either. Card detection already exists in the host: settleQueued's `cardsWaiting = approvals.head() !== undefined || pendingSelections.size > 0` (chat-panel.ts:614) and selection-request tracking (:1456-1457).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The protocol additions go into HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES / WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES at the cited lines, which existing protocol tests check as additive","evidence":"protocol.ts:309 `export const HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES = [`, :325 `export const WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES = [`. protocol.test.ts asserts that prior kinds are still present and that there are no duplicates (lines 113-120), so new types only extend the lists.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A fresh file can be created at version 2 with waiting_on through SCHEMA, and a version-1 file can be upgraded with ALTER TABLE inside the open transaction","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:297-306 runs every SCHEMA statement (`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`) inside write() (BEGIN IMMEDIATE) and writes schema_version only when it is missing. That is why the LLD needs a separate ALTER for an existing version-1 file: IF NOT EXISTS will not add the column. An ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN of a nullable TEXT in that same transaction is sound. insert() names its columns explicitly (:331) and rowToMessage reads by name (:213-239), so older rows stay readable with waiting_on NULL.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A window on the previous plugin that opens a version-2 file falls back to running messages directly, with a notice","evidence":"chat-queue-setup.ts:84-91: when createChatQueueStore throws, the factory logs 'not available, messages run directly', calls notify with 'The chat queue was made by a newer insrc plugin; reload this window. Messages run as before.' for /newer plugin/, and returns undefined. The host then runs without the queue. An old-plugin window that is already open keeps its connection: its SELECT * ignores the extra column and its INSERT names its columns. This is compatible, but the LLD does not say so.","action":"Optional: state that already-open previous-plugin windows keep using the upgraded file, since they check the version only at open.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The changes to s1-owned contracts (sc4 act and onWaiting; sc1 resendFrom, markWaiting and the waiting_on column with the version bump) are proposed as HLD amendments, not redesigned in place","evidence":"Open questions §11 lists the four as HLD amendments. The untracked .insrc/artifacts/AMD-613abdb351c2c738-{3,4,7,8}.json each mention markWaiting / resendFrom / onWaiting / act. HLD.md:184 makes s2 the owner of sc5, and HLD.md:211 assigns blockedBy to s2. s3 takeover, s4 retry logic and s5 review-pane routing are left to their owners (retry-now is a no-op).","action":"Approve the four amendments before this LLD so sc1/sc4 match.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"StoreBusy from cancel or dismiss is caught by worker.act, because the store's cancel and dismiss do not catch it themselves","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:407-413: cancel and dismiss call write() directly, and write throws StoreBusy on SQLITE_BUSY (:274, :288). The LLD says act catches StoreBusy and StoreUnavailable and returns { ok:false, note: BUSY_NOTE or the unavailable note }. BUSY_NOTE is exported at :172. resend/resendFrom already catch it internally (:433-436).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A waiting card that holds a running queued message ends by an answer or by CONTINUATION_WAIT_MS as 'stopped', so the waiting_on flag is cleared when finish rewrites or deletes the row","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:614-624: settleQueued arms waitTimer for continuationWaitMs and ends 'stopped' with 'no answer to the approval'. finish (chat-queue-store.ts:384-404) deletes the row on done or detached-ended, or sets it to failed. Since markWaiting writes only on a processing row, a failed row's stale waiting_on is never projected (projectOutbox reads waitingOn only from processing rows). The LLD's 'ends with the row' holds as long as projectOutbox ignores waitingOn on non-processing rows, which its postcondition states.","action":"Optional: have finish also clear waiting_on so a resent or failed row never carries it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac1-ac4 maps to at least one named test at the right level, using the existing store/worker test fixtures","evidence":"The §6 acceptance mapping lists projection, host and worker/store tests for ac1-ac4. The fixtures named exist: chat-queue-store.test.ts and chat-queue-worker.test.ts already use real temp SQLite files and fake timers. tempQueue() exists at chat-panel.test.ts:34, but it is a local, unexported function. The new chat-queue-outbox-host.test.ts must define its own copy or have it extracted, as chat-queue-routing.test.ts and chat-queue-runner.test.ts already build their own harnesses.","action":"When building, extract tempQueue into a shared test helper or copy it into chat-queue-outbox-host.test.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":15,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-14T12:43:54.657Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
